ty. B is edge-to-edge: an orange header bar plus a left-column stack of yellow tile-like panels, with a large white void on the right.\n- **Typography:** both use a clean sans-serif. A uses dark navy bold heading text; B uses white bold headings on orange and black headings/figures on yellow.\n- **Shared traits:** same 1280×720 dimensions, flat design with no shadows or gradients, and plain sans-serif body text with no images, charts, or icons.\n- **Not shared:** shapes, numbers (A has only the \"K7M4\" alphanumeric marker; B has the numbers 12, 84, 24), colors, and overall composition are all different. Neither file appears to be a variant of the other; they are two unrelated designs."}]}
